 (valid numbers)←max ParseSelectNumbers text;⎕IO;⎕ML;tokens;token;bool;values;lo;hi
⍝ Interprets `text` as the item numbers a user entered for `Select`: single numbers and ranges like
⍝ `3-6` (for `3 4 5 6`), separated by spaces and/or commas, so `1 2,5 10-13` stands for
⍝ `1 2 5 10 11 12 13`.\\
⍝ A range must not contain spaces, both of its numbers must be integers of at least 1, and the second
⍝ one must be greater than the first one: `3 - 6`, `3 -6`, `3- 6` and `5-5` are all invalid.\\
⍝ `max` is the number of choices. A range is expanded no further than `max+1`: that is enough for the
⍝ caller to recognize a range that reaches beyond the choices, and a huge range cannot exhaust the
⍝ workspace.\\
⍝ Returns a Boolean `valid` and, if that is 1, the `numbers` in the order they were entered, duplicates
⍝ included. Whether they are in range is the caller's business, because the user and `a~` are not
⍝ treated the same in that respect.
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 valid←0
 numbers←⍬
 tokens←' '(≠⊆⊢)' '@(','∘=),text
 :For token :In tokens
     :If '-'∊token
         :If 1≠+/'-'=token
         :OrIf '-'∊(⊃token),⊃⌽token
             numbers←⍬ ⋄ :Return
         :EndIf
         (bool values)←⎕VFI' '@('-'∘=)token
         :If ~∧/bool
         :OrIf ∨/values≠⌊values
         :OrIf 1>⊃values
         :OrIf ≥/values
             numbers←⍬ ⋄ :Return
         :EndIf
         (lo hi)←values⌊1+max
         numbers,←(lo-1)↓⍳hi
     :Else
         (bool values)←⎕VFI token
         :If ~∧/bool
             numbers←⍬ ⋄ :Return
         :EndIf
         numbers,←values
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
 valid←1
⍝Done
